You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-c72cd9f9d1ad4b3997162b2b750690e4/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -au Individual`.

## Project Structure
- **Server project**: `/tmp/sv-c72cd9f9d1ad4b3997162b2b750690e4/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/`
- **Client project**: `/tmp/sv-c72cd9f9d1ad4b3997162b2b750690e4/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/`
- **Solution**: `/tmp/sv-c72cd9f9d1ad4b3997162b2b750690e4/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.sln`

## Key Architecture Rules (Auto Mode)
- Interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project
- Interactive components cannot use DbContext directly — they must use HTTP APIs via service interfaces
- Both server and client `Program.cs` must register matching service implementations
- Server implementation uses direct data access; client implementation uses HttpClient
- Don't add `@rendermode` to Identity/Account pages
- Don't set `@rendermode` on `<Routes>` in `App.razor` (per-page mode)

## What to Implement

### 1. Shared Model — create in `.Client` project (referenced by both)

Create `/tmp/sv-c72cd9f9d1ad4b3997162b2b750690e4/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 2. Service Interface — in `.Client` project

Create `/tmp/sv-c72cd9f9d1ad4b3997162b2b750690e4/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
